  (@custom "contractspecv0" (after data) "\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\b1Remove liquidity. Returns `positionMarginRequirement`.\0a`caller` must be the account owner or the collateral engine (liquidation).\0aLiquidations skip the margin check (returns 0).\00\00\00\00\00\00\04burn\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07pool_id\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\06PoolId\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07account\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\07Account\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0atick_lower\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0atick_upper\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0a\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\0a\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\b4Add liquidity. Returns `(positionMarginRequirement, feeIncurred)`.\0a`caller` must be the account owner.\0a\0a`initial_price` sets the pool's price when it was created without one (see\0a[`create_pool`](Self::create_pool)): the first mint must pass `Some(price)`, which\0ainitializes the pool and emits `PoolInitialized`. Once the price is set, mints must\0apass `None` \e2\80\94 supplying a price to an already-priced pool errors with `PriceAlreadySet`.\00\00\00\04mint\00\00\00\07\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07pool_id\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\06PoolId\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07account\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\07Account\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0atick_lower\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0atick_upper\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0a\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dinitial_price\00\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0cSqrtPriceX96\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\0a\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\c8Execute a swap. `amount_specified > 0` = fixed taker, `< 0` = variable taker.\0a`caller` must be the account owner or the collateral engine (liquidation).\0aLiquidations skip the margin check (returns 0).\00\00\00\04swap\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07pool_id\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\06PoolId\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06params\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aSwapParams\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aSwapResult\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\12The current admin.\00\00\00\00\00\05admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\001Derive a pool's id from its key (`PoolKey.toId`).\00\00\00\00\00\00\07pool_id\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\03key\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\07PoolKey\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\06PoolId\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00HReplace the contract's wasm (admin-gated). Address and storage are kept.\00\00\00\07upgrade\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dnew_wasm_hash\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09get_admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\f5Transfer the admin role to `new_admin` (current admin only). The deploy hands the VAMM over\0ato the governance timelock this way once its owner-driven setup has run; afterwards every\0aadmin change (including `create_pool`) goes through governance.\00\00\00\00\00\00\09set_admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09new_admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\88Every pool id ever created, in creation order. The on-chain directory: lets a\0aclient enumerate pools and then drive `mint`/`burn`/`swap` by id alone.\0a\0aReads the whole registry in one call, so it is eventually bounded by the transaction read\0abudget. Clients that must not inherit that bound should page through\0a[`list_pools_page`](Self::list_pools_page) using [`pool_count`](Self::pool_count).\00\00\00\0alist_pools\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\06PoolId\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00FHow many pools have ever been created \e2\80\94 the length of the directory.\00\00\00\00\00\0apool_count\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\91Create and initialize a new pool (admin only). Returns `(tick, poolId)`.\0a`key` fully identifies the pool.\0a\0a`sqrt_price` may be `None` to defer the initial price: the pool is created without a\0aprice (and without a meaningful tick), and the first [`mint`](Self::mint) must supply\0aone. When deferred, the returned tick is `None` and the `PoolInitialized` event fires\0afrom that first mint instead of here.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bcreate_pool\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\03key\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\07PoolKey\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0asqrt_price\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0cSqrtPriceX96\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\02\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\05\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\06PoolId\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00UStorage/schema version, bumped by a post-`upgrade` migration when the layout changes.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bget_version\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00$Whether a pool with this key exists.\00\00\00\0bpool_exists\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\03key\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\07PoolKey\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\96Reconstruct a pool's `PoolKey` from its stored state \e2\80\94 the inverse of\0a[`pool_id`](Self::pool_id). Useful to label/identify a pool given only its id.\00\00\00\00\00\0cget_pool_key\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07pool_id\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\06PoolId\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\07PoolKey\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00LSet global config: the admin (pool creator) and the shared CollateralEngine.\00\00\00\0d__constructor\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06engine\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\000`(tick, sqrtPrice, compoundToken)` for the pool.\00\00\00\0eget_vamm_state\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07pool_id\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\06PoolId\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\05\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0cSqrtPriceX96\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\dbOne page of the directory, in creation order: ids `page * 256 .. (page + 1) * 256`. Empty\0apast the end. Pair with [`pool_count`](Self::pool_count) to walk the registry at a fixed\0acost per call, however many pools exist.\00\00\00\00\0flist_pools_page\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04page\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\06PoolId\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00The `amount_specified` that retires exactly `variable_tokens` of a position's variable leg,\0asigned the same way \e2\80\94 pass a position's `variable_token_balance` to get the notional that\0acloses it out to zero.\0a\0aA swap is quoted in notional and books `ceil(notional / (1 + accrued))` of the pool's\0aterm-start-anchored tokens, so the two units are not interchangeable once the term is under\0away, and a caller cannot compute the inverse off-chain: `accrued` advances with the ledger,\0aso any notional derived before the transaction lands is stale on arrival and leaves a\0aresidue. Worse, retrying against the residue leaves `1 / (1 + accrued)` of it each time \e2\80\94\0ageometric, never reaching the zero that gates a full close.\0a\0aThe floor here is what makes the round trip exact rather than approximate:\0a`ceil(floor(B * (1 + accrued)) / (1 + accrued)) == B` for every `B`, because flooring loses\0astrictly less than one unit and the swap's ceiling puts it back. Rounding the other way would\0aovershoot and flip the leg past zero.\0a\0aRefresh\00\00\00\11notional_to_close\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07pool_id\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\06PoolId\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fvariable_tokens\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\ffThe APR oracle this pool reads its variable factor from and pins `term_start` on \e2\80\94 the\0aengine's own, resolved at [`create_pool`](Self::create_pool). Exposed so a deployment can be\0achecked against the engine's config without a trade having to fail first.\00\00\00\00\13get_pool_apr_oracle\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07pool_id\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\06PoolId\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\03\02Remove liquidity as a liquidation step, driven by the collateral engine. Same pool\0amutation as [`burn`](Self::burn), but returns the resulting `UpdatePositionParams`\0ainstead of calling back into the engine: the engine \e2\80\94 already on the call stack inside\0aits own `liquidate_position` \e2\80\94 applies the update to itself in-process\0a(`update_position_post_vamm_action`). This is what keeps the engine from re-entering\0aitself through the VAMM (engine -> vamm -> engine), which the two-hop `burn` callback\0awould otherwise require during liquidation. `caller` must be the configured engine; the\0amargin check `burn` runs is meaningless here (liquidations are forced closes), so it is\0askipped. The engine is the only intended caller \e2\80\94 see `CollateralEngine::liquidate_position`.\00\00\00\00\00\14burn_for_liquidation\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07pool_id\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\06PoolId\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07account\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\07Account\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0atick_lower\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0atick_upper\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0a\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\14UpdatePositionParams\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\015Execute a swap as a liquidation step, driven by the collateral engine. Same pool math as\0a[`swap`](Self::swap), but returns the resulting `UpdatePositionParams` instead of calling\0aback into the engine \e2\80\94 see\0a[`burn_for_liquidation`](Self::burn_for_liquidation) for why. `caller` must be the\0aconfigured engine.\00\00\00\00\00\00\14swap_for_liquidation\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07pool_id\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\06PoolId\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06params\00\00\00\00\07\d0\0